     `if !m.HasCombinedTarget { return v }`), so "HasTarget false with
     IsOver true" cannot occur — confirmed by code, not assumed.
   - -0 hazard: formatMoney (render.go:432) normalizes `v==0` to `+0`
     before the sign check (pre-existing CB7 belt) — protects both the
     lead's abs() branch and the tile's raw $flow.Balance branch
     identically, so "matched" (Balance==0) can never render "-$0.00" on
     either surface.
   - Rendered a live "did not cover" case (2026-07-01..2026-08-27 on the
     verify-server data copy, port 8148): lead said "$4,955.75 under plan
     ... did not cover spending by $11,359.69"; Budget tile independently
     showed "$4,955.75 under"; Cash-flow tile showed "-$11,359.69" —
     figures agree exactly, sign-normalized.
   - Fixture-math for the "matched" case: verified 10.001/9.999 ->
     ReportingCashFlow rounds Income/Spending to cents FIRST then
     subtracts, giving Balance exactly 0 (go test confirms "$0.00" /
     "Recorded income matches spending"); this is ruling RF-2026-09-07b's
     documented correction of the original spec fixture math (10.006/
     10.004 would NOT match) — the worker's test uses the corrected pair.

